Hi,

this series reverts the "consolidate DCN vblank/flip handling onto
vupdate_no_lock" change (c87e6635d2db) and its two follow-ups, which cause
frequent, short bursts of visual corruption on a gfx1201 multi-monitor
setup. The known follow-up fix (70de0a021658, "Atomize IRQ register
read/modify/write ops", which closes #5616) does NOT cover this failure
mode - the corruption there is not accompanied by any flip_done timeouts,
and it remains with the fix applied.

Symptom: brief (~0.1s) bursts of white-noise strips on ALL connected
displays simultaneously, nearly constant within minutes of normal Wayland
desktop use, in a mixed-timing dual-monitor configuration
(3840x2160@144 DP + 1920x1080@60 HDMI). Kernel log is completely quiet at
the events. This is visually distinct from #5616's freezes/flip_done
timeouts - I believe it is an unreported second failure mode of the same
commit.

Evidence (module-level test builds against distro 7.0.0-38 headers,
vermagic- and CRC-identical to stock, only amdgpu.ko/ttm.ko swapped):

   without the commit (older kernel state) .................. clean 
(>=10 min)
   with the commit .......................................... glitchy 
(~1/6s)
   commit + follow-ups reverted ............................. clean (hours)
   commit kept, only follow-ups reverted .................... glitchy
   commit kept + 70de0a021658 applied ....................... glitchy

Also ruled out: DCC / explicit modifiers (reproduces with
WLR_EGL_NO_MODIFIERS=1 and radeonsi R600_DEBUG=nodcc), DPM clock
transitions (mclk sits pinned at its top level in this configuration and
per-clock-domain transition statistics are identical in glitch and
glitch-free windows), firmware age (linux-firmware HEAD), VRR (off),
display link and engine (TTY console at identical modes is clean), and
hardware (Windows clean for weeks at identical timings).

Full report and raw data: 
https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/drm/amd/-/issues/6004

I understand a blanket revert may undo intended vblank-timing improvements,
so if you prefer a targeted change (e.g. falling back to the legacy vblank
IRQ source for multi-CRTC / mixed-timing configurations), I can turn that
around quickly and test it: my build+reproducibility loop is minutes, and
the glitch is near-constant when present, so results are decisive within a
5-minute test session.

Thanks,
Ava H

